# Sound assets directory for RustRide audio engine
#
# Place WAV or MP3 sound files here. The audio backend will load
# them by name (without extension).
#
# SOUND FILE CATALOG
# ==================
#
# Countdown Sounds:
# - countdown_tick.wav - Short tick for each countdown second
# - countdown_3.wav - 3 seconds remaining (higher pitch)
# - countdown_2.wav - 2 seconds remaining (even higher)
# - countdown_1.wav - 1 second remaining (highest, most urgent)
# - countdown_go.wav - Go! Interval starting now
#
# Interval Sounds:
# - interval_warning.wav - Interval change approaching
# - interval_change.wav - Interval has changed
# - interval_rest.wav - Rest interval started
# - interval_work.wav - Work interval started
#
# Achievement Sounds:
# - achievement_bronze.wav - Bronze achievement unlocked (simple chime)
# - achievement_silver.wav - Silver achievement unlocked (richer harmony)
# - achievement_gold.wav - Gold achievement unlocked (triumphant fanfare)
# - achievement_platinum.wav - Platinum achievement unlocked (epic celebration)
# - level_up.wav - Level up notification
#
# Milestone Sounds:
# - milestone_distance.wav - Distance milestone (5km, 10km, etc.)
# - milestone_time.wav - Time milestone (15min, 30min, etc.)
# - milestone_calories.wav - Calorie milestone
# - personal_record.wav - Personal record achieved
#
# Workout Lifecycle Sounds:
# - workout_start.wav - Workout is starting
# - workout_pause.wav - Workout paused
# - workout_resume.wav - Workout resumed
# - workout_complete.wav - Workout completed successfully
# - workout_stop.wav - Workout stopped early
#
# Zone Change Sounds:
# - zone_up.wav - Entering higher power zone
# - zone_down.wav - Entering lower power zone
#
# Alert Sounds:
# - notification.wav - General notification
# - warning.wav - Warning alert
# - error.wav - Error alert
# - success.wav - Success confirmation
#
# Connection Sounds:
# - device_connected.wav - Device connected
# - device_disconnected.wav - Device disconnected
#
# FALLBACK BEHAVIOR
# =================
# If any audio file is missing, the audio engine will automatically
# generate appropriate tones as fallback. See src/audio/sounds.rs
# for the fallback tone definitions.
#
# AUDIO FILE REQUIREMENTS
# =======================
# - Format: WAV (recommended) or MP3
# - Sample rate: 44100 Hz recommended
# - Duration: Keep sounds short (<500ms for notifications, <200ms for ticks)
# - Volume: Normalize to -3dB peak for consistent playback
